NAME
     mkfs_ext4 - make an ext4 file system

SYNOPSIS
     mkfs.ext4 [-b BLOCKS] [-j BLOCKS] [-L LABEL] DEVICE

DESCRIPTION
     mkfs.ext4 writes an empty ext4 file system: the superblock, the
     group descriptors, the bitmaps, the inode table, the root directory
     and a journal.

OPTIONS
     -b BLOCKS   how many blocks of 4096 bytes
     -j BLOCKS   the journal's size in blocks
     -L LABEL    the volume label

SEE ALSO
     mount(1), e2tools(8), mkimage(1), blkid(8)
